; Still water that freezes in a hard frost (read by src/weather.c at boot).
;
; One room vnum, or a range "<first>-<last>", per line.  Only outdoor water
; rooms (sector 6 or 7) in these ranges count, so a range may cover a whole
; lake.  Lines starting with ';' are comments; the file ends with '$'.
;
; Each zone's ice thickens by 1 an hour at -5 degrees or colder and thins by
; 2 an hour above freezing (0-6).  At 4 the water bears weight: it can be
; walked on without a boat, players there are told, 'weather' says so, and
; fishing means chopping a hole.  When it thins to 0 the ice breaks up, and
; anyone on deep water without a boat scrambles to the nearest shore.
; Don't list rivers with a current, or the sea.

